  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The action will address the global objective of enhancing CSO participation in free and independent engagement with a special focus on sustainable, equitable and inclusive natural resources management within a transparent and accountable governance. This will be achieved through strengthening of CSO capacities to: promote evidence-based advocacy and dialogue, improve community engagement in the energy transition and extractive sectors, promote the participation of women and youth CSOs, ensure accountability of government and private sector to national and international standards for access to information, promote community rights and consultations on all levels, connect and interlink CSOs at all levels, and promote knowledge dissemination, coalition building and networking opportunities for CSOs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The action will strengthen the ability of CSOs to advocate for their rights, engage in the GH2 and mining sectors, shape public policy and hold government and the private sector accountable. The action will focus on local, regional and national level CSOs to ensure that they are working together to protect community rights and ensure increased benefits at all levels in a coordinated way.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
